{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"U_kgDOEdrZdw","is_bot":false,"login":"earnestmant2","name":""},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen a MySQL connection is reset (e.g., due to a server-side timeout, TCP reset, or network disruption), the driver detects the failure and returns `driver.ErrBadConn`. The Go `database/sql` standard library automatically intercepts `driver.ErrBadConn` and retries the query on a new connection from the pool.\n\nHowever, if the connection reset occurs after session-specific states have been modified (such as DSN-configured system variables, session collations, or transaction states), the automatic retry on a new connection can lead to inconsistent states. Specifically:\n1. If the driver fails to fully re-initialize DSN-configured session variables (`system_vars`) on the new connection, queries will run with default server settings.\n2. If a connection reset occurs mid-transaction or after a write operation, returning `driver.ErrBadConn` might trigger an unsafe automatic retry of a non-idempotent query.\n3. Internal driver state (such as cached prepared statements or connection flags) may not be properly cleaned up when the connection is marked bad.\n\nWe need to ensure that connection resets are handled safely, session variables are consistently re-applied on retried connections, and `driver.ErrBadConn` is only returned when it is safe to retry the operation.\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] **Safe Retry Logic:** `driver.ErrBadConn` must only be returned if no data has been written to the connection for the current query, or if the connection was lost while idle in the pool. If a write has already occurred, the actual network error must be returned to prevent unsafe retries of non-idempotent operations.\n- [ ] **Session Variable Re-initialization:** Ensure that all DSN-configured session variables (e.g., `system_vars`, `sql_mode`, `time_zone`) are reliably executed and verified during the connection establishment phase of the new connection.\n- [ ] **State Cleanup:** When a connection is marked bad, all associated driver-side resources (e.g., cached prepared statements, transaction state flags) must be explicitly invalidated and cleared.\n- [ ] **Transaction Safety:** If a connection reset occurs during an active transaction, the driver must not return `driver.ErrBadConn` in a way that allows `database/sql` to silently retry the query on a new connection outside of the transaction context.\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\n- **Relevant Files:**\n  - `connection.go`: Manages connection lifecycle, initialization, and state.\n  - `packets.go`: Handles reading/writing packets and error translation.\n  - `driver.go`: Implements the `driver.Driver` and `driver.Connector` interfaces.\n- **Key Functions to Modify/Inspect:**\n  - `mysqlConn.cleanup()`: Ensure it thoroughly invalidates prepared statements and resets internal state flags when a connection is closed or marked bad.\n  - `mysqlConn.handleError()`: Refine the logic that maps network errors (like `syscall.ECONNRESET`, `io.EOF`, or `write: connection reset by peer`) to `driver.ErrBadConn`.\n  - `connector.Connect()`: Verify that the initialization SQL queries (setting up `system_vars`, collation, etc.) are executed atomically before the connection is returned to the pool.\n- **Context:**\n  - Go's `database/sql` package relies on the driver returning `driver.ErrBadConn` to trigger its retry loop. If we return `driver.ErrBadConn` after a query has been partially sent, we risk duplicate execution. We must track whether a write operation has started on the wire for the current command.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\nHunter, please verify the fix using the following testing strategies:\n\n1. **Unit Test for Session Re-initialization:**\n   - Write a test in `connection_test.go` that establishes a connection with custom `system_vars` in the DSN (e.g., `system_vars=sql_mode='ANSI'`).\n   - Force a connection reset on the underlying net.Conn (e.g., by closing the raw TCP connection or using a mock net.Conn).\n   - Execute a subsequent query and assert that the new connection established by the pool successfully re-applies the `sql_mode='ANSI'` setting.\n\n2. **Integration Test for Unsafe Retries:**\n   - Simulate a connection reset mid-write.\n   - Verify that the driver returns the raw network error (or a wrapped error) instead of `driver.ErrBadConn`, preventing `database/sql` from retrying the query.\n\n3. **Mock Server Test:**\n   - Use a mock MySQL server to close the connection immediately after receiving a query header.\n   - Assert that the driver handles the `EOF` / `ECONNRESET` correctly based on whether the query was fully written.\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @earnestmant2</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@earnestmant2</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIrhUCQ","author":{"login":"earnestmant2"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"/reward 10","createdAt":"2026-07-03T14:58:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877472777","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIrhVKw","author":{"login":"opirebot"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"😅 Ups... you cannot create a reward of $10.00. It needs to be at least $20.00","createdAt":"2026-07-03T14:58:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877473067","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIrhZ1A","author":{"login":"dev-nana27"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-07-03T14:58:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877474260","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIriAGA","author":{"login":"Rachaelisa"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #1\n\nI can get this done. Going through the codebase now — the issue looks clear enough. I'll put up a pull request shortly after I've validated the fix.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T15:00:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877484056","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIriC0Q","author":{"login":"Zubi-fix"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #1\n\nHappy to handle this bounty. I'm reviewing the issue details and the relevant modules now — should have a PR up soon once I've run through it locally.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T15:00:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877484753","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIriFnw","author":{"login":"code-cannot-be-blank"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #1\n\nOn it. I'm looking at the issue description and tracing through the code to find the best place for the fix. Will share a PR soon — ping me if there's extra context I should know about.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T15:00:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877485471","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIrpamA","author":{"login":"2lll5"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-07-03T15:19:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877605528","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABIrqZyQ","author":{"login":"2lll5"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Implemented in PR: https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/pull/3","createdAt":"2026-07-03T15:21:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4877621705","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABItlKCQ","author":{"login":"stmr"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I can take this if still available/payable.\n\nPlanned scope: Prevent session state inconsistency on connection reset and ErrBadConn retry.\n\nI will keep the PR/submission focused, include tests/docs where requested, run project checks, and wait for maintainer or bounty-platform confirmation before starting work.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T22:23:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4879632905","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMtZR88AAAABI7r7pw","author":{"login":"dev-nana27"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/try\n\nI can fix the MySQL driver connection reset state inconsistency. The fix involves tracking session-scoped state changes and preventing unsafe automatic retries on non-idempotent queries when `driver.ErrBadConn` is returned after connection reset. I write Go database drivers.<details><summary>Check if you're the only one trying 👇</summary><br/>You're the first one to try to solve this issue, go for it! 😉</details>","createdAt":"2026-07-06T15:14:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1#issuecomment-4894423975","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2026-07-03T14:58:37Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOTMtZR88AAAACqBG6nw","name":"bounty","description":"","color":"ededed"},{"id":"LA_kwDOTMtZR88AAAACqBG6og","name":"opire","description":"","color":"ededed"},{"id":"LA_kwDOTMtZR88AAAACqBG6ow","name":"$10","description":"","color":"ededed"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"🎯 Fix: Prevent Session State Inconsistency on Connection Reset and driver.ErrBadConn Retry","updatedAt":"2026-07-06T15:14:21Z","url":"https://github.com/earnestmant2/mysql/issues/1"}
